Games are supposed to be fun and relaxing, aren't they? Isn't a good game
supposed to accommodate various playing styles, techniques, and skill
levels? I think it's a weakness in the game if the game can only be won by
a particular game strategy or player. For some people, NH 3.0 seems like
the ultimate game (apparently). For a good number of us, though, the game
feels impossibly frustrating and unrewarding. If you want to create a
really good game, you should leave enough flexibility in its structure to
allow each player to play (and win and ENJOY playing) in their own way.
Otherwise, you're just catering to a small group of "experets". Which is
great for them, but hardly adds to the game's popularity in the long run...


